/-
# RFC 8032 Ed25519 — Hostile vectors: adversarial verification cases

Compile with `lake env lean Ed25519Hostile.lean` (with `Ed25519.lean` in
the same source root and the import below).  This file contains no
`sorry`, no `admit` and no `axiom`; every theorem is closed by
`native_decide`.

Contents: the twenty-two adversarial cases of the project ground truth
(`ground_truth.json`, dual-verified against OpenSSL and an independent
pure-Python model).  Nineteen cases must be REJECTED by `verify` (bit
flips, non-canonical scalars, small-order points, truncation/extension,
cross-vector confusion, ...); three are ACCEPT controls proving that the
strict verifier still accepts genuine signatures.  Each case carries its
`adversarial_property` from the ground truth.

For REJECT cases the primary theorem is
`verify pk msg sig = false`; where the rejection is specifically a
decoding/canonicality failure, a companion theorem pins down the
responsible predicate (`isCanonicalS`, `isCanonicalPointEncoding`,
`isSmallOrder`).
-/

import Std
import Ed25519

namespace ProofBundle.Crypto.Ed25519

